# Repository Layer

## Contract

`src/Repositories/IBlingRepository.php` is the only HTTP surface entities depend on. Every method accepts `RequestOptions` and returns `ResponseOptions`.

`RequestOptions` carries `endpoint`, `queryParams` (`QueryParams`, array, or null), `headers`, and `body` (`Body`, array, or null). Resource ids are part of `endpoint`. The repository has no separate id argument.

### Verb mapping (Laravel-style names)

| Method | HTTP | Use in entities |
|--------|------|-----------------|
| `index` | GET | Collection or auxiliary route. A parent id may sit in the path (`campos-customizados/modulos/{idModulo}` in `CamposCustomizados::findByModule`) |
| `show` | GET | One resource (`contatos/{idContato}`, `contatos/consumidor-final`) |
| `store` | POST | Create, and POST actions such as `nfe/{id}/lancar-estoque` |
| `update` | PATCH | Partial update and PATCH actions |
| `replace` | PUT | Full replacement and PUT actions |
| `destroy` | DELETE | Delete one resource or a bulk delete |

`index` and `show` both send GET to `options->endpoint` with the query string and headers. Entities still pick the verb from the table above.

## Implementation

`src/Repositories/BlingRepository.php` builds a Guzzle client with:

- `base_uri` set to the API root
- `'http_errors' => false`, so HTTP 4xx and 5xx are returned as a `ResponseOptions`

Each call merges the bearer header with `$options->headers` and sends `$options->body->content` as JSON on POST, PATCH, PUT, and DELETE. The response body is `json_decode`d to an associative array and wrapped in `Body`. A body that is not a JSON array or object becomes `null` (`buildResponseBody`).

## Normalization

Constructing `ResponseOptions` (`src/Entities/@shared/DTO/Request/ResponseOptions.php`) is the error boundary:

- HTTP status `>= 400`, or a body that contains an `error` key, is parsed as `ErrorResponse`.
- A parsed Bling error becomes `BlingApiException` (message = `error.description`, code = HTTP status).
- A payload that fails `ErrorResponse::from` surfaces as `BlingInternalException`.
- A `\TypeError` during that parse becomes `BlingInternalException` with message `Não foi possível realizar a chamada HTTP: {method} {endpoint}`.

Entity code does not catch Guzzle exceptions and does not inspect status codes.

## Rules for changes

- Add a new HTTP shape only on `IBlingRepository` and `BlingRepository`.
- Keep the verb names. Map a new Bling operation onto the row that matches its HTTP method.
- Leave query keys as PHP names (`idsProdutos`). Do not append `[]` in the library.
